# SupervisorCmd.srv — state-machine control for smb_nodes.supervisor.
#
# Phase 4 (2026-07-27): minimal FSM, only IDLE + ESTOP implemented.
# NAV / DOCK are accepted by the service but are no-ops on the supervisor
# side — the actual Nav2 waypoint sequence runs via the separate
# `waypoint_follower` executable, which is launched by a higher-level
# orchestrator (Android hub or a future BT tree) once the supervisor is in
# NAV. The supervisor does NOT launch waypoint_follower itself: keeping
# single responsibility between this node (state machine) and the nav runner
# (Nav2 client) makes each side independently testable.
#
# Requested `command` values:
#   'idle'   — enter IDLE (pass-through cmd_vel).
#   'nav'    — enter NAV (pass-through cmd_vel; logs informational).
#   'dock'   — enter DOCK (stub: logs "not implemented" and stays IDLE).
#   'estop'  — enter ESTOP (zeroes cmd_vel; emergency stop).
#   'reset'  — leave ESTOP and return to IDLE. Required after estop before
#              any other command is accepted.

string command
string current_state    # echoed back for caller convenience (filled by
                        # service handler in the same call) — set to empty
                        # in the request.

---

bool success
string message           # human-readable status; non-empty on failure.
string new_state         # state the supervisor is in AFTER the call.
